# Reported speech in Russian: he advised us to go
subtitle: "Pass on what someone said, asked, told you to do or advised in Russian: сказа́л, что; спроси́л, ли; сказа́л, что́бы; посове́товал."
tags: ["russian","reported speech","посоветовал","golden ring","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/reported-speech","grammar/indirect-questions","vocabulary/travel"]
thumb: "band \"He advised us to go\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Even if in Russian: даже если, всё-таки, что бы ни","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/146-russian-even-if.cast"}

